@format 1
@id media-loading.in-staged-workspace
@title In staged workspace
@section Media loading
@area In staged workspace
@entry staged-run
@summary Show the staged-processing path that loads already planned media paths directly into a temporary workspace Files docket.
@related media-loading.common.docket-insertion
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag staging

@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket

[staged-run] Cartographer staged-workspace execution <input>
~ This starts with cartographer staged-workspace execution.
[Technical explanation]
- Construct a temporary PWorkspace for the planned layout and obtain its action and Files surfaces @ workspace.PWorkspaceStageRun(...)
> staged-surface

[staged-surface] Staged Files surface available <decision>
~ The program checks whether the temporary workspace has a Files list.
[Technical explanation]
- Require both an action surface and Files list before loading the planned media paths @ workspace.PWorkspaceStageRun(...)
? "Action and Files available" > staged-add
? "Required surface missing" > staged-rejected

[staged-add] Load planned paths directly into staged Files <process>
~ This step handles load planned paths directly into staged Files.
[Technical explanation]
- Pass the planned paths directly to LDocketPathsAdd with the planned batch and delivered=true; PWorkspaceStageRun does not call PListMediaScan or PListPathsAdd @ workspace.PWorkspaceStageRun(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
> staged-loaded

[staged-rejected] Staged media not loaded <output>
~ This path ends with staged media not loaded.
[Technical explanation]
= The temporary workspace lacks a required surface, so no docket insertion occurs.

[staged-loaded] Planned media loaded into temporary program state <output>
~ This path ends with planned media loaded into temporary program state.
[Technical explanation]
= The planned paths have been offered directly to the staged workspace docket; subsequent staged processing is outside this media-intake map.
